<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Correo del Orinoco</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1818–1822</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Correo del <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orinoco">Orinoco</a> was a newspaper published at Angostura, now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ciudad-bolivar">Ciudad Bolívar</a>, from 1818 to 1822 by the patriot government of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simon-bolivar">Simón Bolívar</a>. It promoted the cause of independence, printed official decrees and news of the war, and answered royalist propaganda. It is regarded as a founding work of Venezuelan journalism.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/correo-del-orinoco.jpg" alt="Correo del Orinoco" width="320" height="451" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Correo_del_Orinoco_1818_000.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
